I'm suspicious of this fix — `runes` is only `true` if the write happens inside an effect in a runes-mode context. It's `false` if, for example, the write happens in an event handler — given the basic demo app...

```svelte
<script>
  let count = $state(0);

  function increment() {
    count += 1;
  }
</script>

<button onclick={increment}>
  clicks: {count}
</button>
```

...if you add a `console.log({ runes })` inside `mark_reactions` then it will log `{ runes: false }` every time you click the button. It feels like this change would result in a very significant amount of unnecessary work.
